# The browsers the client bundle is compiled and prefixed for.
#
# This is Next's own default list, the one it hands SWC, written down because
# Babel does the compiling now and Babel does not know about it: `next/babel`
# leaves `@babel/preset-env` to ask browserslist, and preset-env with no list to
# find compiles for nothing in particular, which means ES5. That cost 1.4MB of
# extra JavaScript across the bundle and put every `await` in the app through a
# regenerator shim. Nothing in the port asked for it and no measurement of the
# port is honest without it.
#
# Autoprefixer reads the same list, so the stylesheet is prefixed for the
# browsers the JavaScript is built for rather than for browserslist's defaults.
#
# It lives at the repo root rather than in `frontend/` because the file a build
# picks up depends on which directory it started in, and `pnpm --filter frontend
# build`, a Vercel build and an editor plugin do not agree on that. See
# `docs/stylex.md`.
chrome 64
edge 79
firefox 67
opera 51
safari 12
